+/// pokezero gen3 fidelity fix (G8, roll-dependent Leech Seed drain).
+///
+/// The 16 gen 3 damage rolls of a fan, in EXACT INTEGER arithmetic:
+/// `floor(max * r / 100)` for `r` in `85..=100`. Character-for-character the
+/// expression `push_enumerated_rolls` uses, which is itself the expression the
+/// already-shipped 32-arm `pending_hp_reading_move` enumeration in this same
+/// function uses -- so this generalises arithmetic the engine already runs in
+/// production rather than inventing a second convention.
+///
+/// Deliberately NOT the f32 accumulator `compare_health_with_damage_multiples`
+/// walks (`max * 0.85` stepped by `max * 0.01`). That one drifts below the true
+/// rung on some fans -- C116 M5 -- and a drifted value is a damage amount
+/// Showdown can never deal, so an arm priced at it can only miss. Using the
+/// integer fan means that WHENEVER the split fires, every roll Showdown could
+/// actually have thrown inside the band has an arm at exactly that value.
+///
+/// The cost of not sharing the comparator's basis is that the two can disagree
+/// about how many rolls a band holds. `push_per_roll_residual_kill_arms` checks
+/// that count and declines to split when it differs, so a drifted band keeps the
+/// single collapsed arm it emits today -- INCLUDING the case where that arm
+/// happens to sit on the roll Showdown threw. The split is therefore a strict
+/// improvement or a no-op on any given band, never a trade.
+///
+/// Rolls that collapse onto the same integer (small `max`) are NOT merged here:
+/// each of the sixteen carries 1/16 of the fan either way, and
+/// `combine_duplicate_instructions` at the end of
+/// `generate_instructions_from_move` folds identical arms back together with
+/// their masses summed. Keeping all sixteen slots is also what makes the count
+/// comparable to the comparator's, which is likewise out of sixteen.
+fn residual_band_roll_fan(max_damage: i16) -> [i16; 16] {
+    let mut fan = [0i16; 16];
+    for (index, slot) in fan.iter_mut().enumerate() {
+        *slot = (max_damage as i32 * (85 + index as i32) / 100) as i16;
+    }
+    fan
+}
